#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gametype:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arcade"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "Number of possible players:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multiplayer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&granatier; is a clone of the classic <trademark><application>Bomberman</"
"application></trademark> game, inspired by the work of the "
"<application>Clanbomber</application> clone."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The object of the game is to run through an arena, using bombs to clear out "
"blocks and eliminate your opponents. Several bonuses and handicaps are "
"hidden underneath the blocks &ndash; these can either help or hinder your "
"progress."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>A &granatier; screenshot</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>A &granatier; screenshot</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Objective:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Eliminate all Opponents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each player is provided with five keys that they use to move their character "
"and lay bombs. For example, the default keys for Player 1 are the Up, Down, "
"Left and Right arrow keys to move respectively in those directions, and the "
"&Enter; key to lay a bomb. Please refer to the <link linkend=\"config_player"
"\">Player Configuration</link> Section to find shortcut keys for other "
"players, as well as how to configure them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The purpose of laying bombs, aside from attacking other opponents, is to "
"destroy the many blocks scattered throughout the arena in order to clear a "
"path or uncover hidden bonuses. Among the many bonuses that can be uncovered "
"are those that make you move faster or increase your bomb blast range; the "
"more bonuses of this type you collect, the easier it is to eliminate your "
"opponents and win the round. But be warned that just as many handicaps exist "
"that can turn the tide against you, including those that slow you down or "
"invert your moving keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each won round, the player is awarded a point. The first player to win a "
"predefined number of points (the default is 3), wins the game!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules, Strategies and Tips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Items"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Arena"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "The players are in an arena which consists of:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arena Wall"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Wall &ndash; this defines the outline of the arena map and cannot be "
"destroyed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arena Ground"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Ground &ndash; this can be walked on safely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arena Ice"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Ice &ndash; this will make the ground slippery. The speed increases on "
"the ice and it is not possible to completly stop moving."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arena Block"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Block &ndash; this can be destroyed with a bomb, and may contain a bonus "
"(or a handicap)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arena Bomb Mortar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Bomb Mortar &ndash; this will throw bombs that are placed on it to "
"random places."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arena Arrow Right"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Arrows &ndash; this will move the bombs that are placed on it to the "
"direction they point."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is none of the above items, there is a hole at the ground and "
"moving into it will result in falling into the deep and die. The same "
"applies also if there is no wall at the edge of the arena and the player "
"moves outside of the arena."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Bonuses"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Bonuses are helpful for reaching the game goal and effects exists permanent "
"- even after a handicap disappears. Currently there are following bonuses:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Speed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Speed &ndash; increases your speed slightly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Bomb"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Bomb &ndash; adds an extra bomb to your arsenal, allowing you to lay more "
"than one bomb at a time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Power"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Power &ndash; increases the power of your bombs, extending their bomb blast "
"range."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Shield"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shield &ndash; makes invincible for one bomb blast."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Throw"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Throw &ndash; adds the ability to throw bombs. Just press the key for laying "
"bombs while a bomb is below you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Kick"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Kick &ndash; adds the ability to move bombs. Just run against an bomb and "
"the bomb will move."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Handicaps"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Handicaps are the opposite of bonuses and hinder the player. The good thing "
"is that effects get lost after some time (other than bonuses) and the player "
"can play in is usual behavior (including bonuses) again. Currently there are "
"following handicaps:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Handicap Slow"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Slow &ndash; makes you move very slowly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "Handicap Hyperactive"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hyperactive &ndash; makes you move a little TOO fast."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid "Handicap Mirror"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mirror &ndash; inverts your moving keys, so that up becomes down and left "
"becomes right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Handicap Scatty"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scatty &ndash; forces you to continuously lay bombs without control."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "Handicap Restrain"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restrain &ndash; prevents you to lay bombs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "The ambivalent Items"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This type of bonuses are neither good nor bad, it mostly depends on the "
"environment. Currently there are following neutral bonuses:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Neutral Pandora"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pandora &ndash; this contains either a bonus or a handicap."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bonus Neutral Resurrect"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resurrect &ndash; this will resurrect any dead player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:245
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open the Configuration Dialogue, select <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &granatier;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the points which are needed to win the game and the time for "
"a round. After the time is over, the sudden death mode will start."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additionally you can adjust the initial speed, bomb range and bomb armory."
msgstr ""

